  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts five women in swimsuits on a beach, juxtaposed with text that reads 'all those in favour of bringing swedish women to america as refugees instead of muslims please like and share.' This meme uses the visual representation of attractive, Western women to imply a preference for them over Muslim refugees, suggesting a discriminatory hierarchy based on gender, nationality, and religion. The text explicitly frames a choice between two groups, implying that one group (Swedish women) is preferable to the other (Muslims), which constitutes a hateful message targeting Muslim refugees. The meme promotes xenophobia and Islamophobia by dehumanizing and ranking refugees based on superficial and nationalistic criteria, and it encourages engagement ('like and share') to spread this discriminatory sentiment. The overall intent is to incite prejudice and hostility toward Muslim refugees by associating them with negative stereotypes and contrasting them with an idealized image of Swedish women, thereby promoting a harmful and hateful worldview.",
